+## Follow-up passes, 2026-11-05
+
+**No new official county source was verified. Coverage remains 13 configured counties and
+69 unresolved counties.** Each unresolved county has `followup_passes` records in the JSON
+inventory. The record lists the pages checked and the outcome.
+
+- **16:22Z, restricted session.** Only a search engine was available. The SOS results page
+  listed only the March 10, 2026 primaries; certified November results are expected around
+  December 3. Statewide report-text searches found only counties already configured
+  (DeSoto, Warren).
+- **16:48Z, unrestricted network.** Each known county, circuit clerk and election commission
+  page was requested once, plus one level of election links. WordPress and CivicPlus listings
+  were checked for items published after November 2. No challenge, block or TLS error was
+  bypassed.
+
+| Outcome | Counties | Evidence and next action |
+|---|---|---|
+| Requires human review (2) | Lee, Benton | **Lee:** the official site returned 503 or reset the connection. A Daily Journal story relays Senate counts from unofficial circuit clerk results; that is not admissible, so request the original. **Benton:** the official results page renders client-side (Wix) with no 2026 report in its HTML; check it in a browser. |
+| Wrong election (4) | Bolivar, Jackson, Pearl River, Washington | Results pages hold only older elections. **Pearl River:** the county-linked ArcGIS app was retitled "General Election 2026", but its data sources are a 2023 primary map, a deleted service, and a precinct layer last edited 2023-11-08. |
+| Blocked (20) | Adams, Calhoun, Chickasaw, Claiborne, Clarke, Copiah, Harrison, Holmes, Jefferson Davis, Leflore, Marion, Newton, Pontotoc, Smith, Stone, Tippah, Tishomingo, Walthall, Webster, Wilkinson | No official page was retrievable. Causes were HTTP 403 (Harrison, every page), HTTP 503, connection resets, DNS failures, or TLS errors (for example, Tippah's certificate does not match its host). Retry from another network or ask the circuit clerk. |
+| Not found (38) | Alcorn, Amite, Attala, Carroll, Clay, Coahoma, Covington, Forrest, Franklin, George, Greene, Humphreys, Jasper, Jefferson, Jones, Kemper, Lawrence, Leake, Lincoln, Lowndes, Marshall, Montgomery, Noxubee, Oktibbeha, Panola, Perry, Prentiss, Quitman, Scott, Sharkey, Simpson, Tate, Tunica, Union, Wayne, Winston, Yalobusha, Yazoo | Reachable official pages had no November 2026 Senate report. Lincoln's "Election Central" link (`dustinbairfield.com`) now serves gambling spam: it is not an authority, and the county may want to know. Franklin's only lead returns 404. |
+| No known site (5) | Choctaw, Grenada, Issaquena, Itawamba, Tallahatchie | Only the SOS directory contact is known. |
+
+**Configured but blocked: Hancock.** Hancock's configured PDF was captured at 02:14Z on
+November 5 (SHA-256 `95c3086e…`, Colom 4,538 / Hyde-Smith 11,441 / Pinkins 753, 26 of 26
+precincts). By about 22:00Z the same URL returned HTTP 403 with a Cloudflare "Sorry, you
+have been blocked" page, both from the development workspace and from the production host.
+Production has never collected it. The block is not bypassed. Ask the county or CivicPlus to
+allow the pipeline, or import the file as a manual snapshot (see *A configured URL the host
+cannot fetch* in [collection and intake](mississippi-collection.md)).
+
+Absence is a point-in-time observation: counties often post reports days after the election,
+or only on social media. Adding a county still requires its original official report captured
+with exact bytes and a SHA-256. See *Onboarding a county* in
+[collection and intake](mississippi-collection.md).
+
 ## Expansion checkpoint
 
 Lafayette, Lamar and Sunflower were added to the configured reports. See [collection and intake](mississippi-collection.md) for exact source limitations and the reviewed-file process for the remaining 69 counties. Historical probe outcomes above retain their original timestamps; absence of a report in that pass does not prove that none exists. The machine-readable `intake` field is the current implementation status for each county.
